    },
    {
      "line": 10,
      "type": "scene_header",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "line": 11,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "unknown",
      "text": "\"Those who choose honor,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 12,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Elder Pazuzu declared, his ancient form beginning to glow with the accumulated power of eons, \"will stand with me. We will face the Anunnaki as our ancestors faced the Void-Spawn. We will remind them that the Igigi do not yield.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 14,
      "type": "dialogue",
      "speaker": "Zephyr",
      "text": "\"Those who choose survival,\""
    },
    {
      "line": 16,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "For a moment that stretched across probability space, the choice hung in perfect balance."
    },
    {
      "line": 17,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Honor or survival."
    },
    {
      "line": 18,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Glory or continuity."
    },
    {
      "line": 19,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The fire that burns bright and dies, or the ember that endures through darkness."
    },
    {
      "line": 21,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Ishara was the first to move, her young form flowing toward the transport pods."
    },
    {
      "line": 22,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"I choose tomorrow,\" she said simply."
    },
    {
      "line": 23,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "\"Whatever tomorrow looks like.\""
    },
    {
      "line": 25,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "One by one, others followed."
    },
    {
      "line": 26,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not all—Elder Pazuzu and nearly a third of the council remained, their forms beginning to resonate with the harmonics of final battle."
    },
    {
      "line": 27,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But the majority chose Zephyr's path."
    },
    {
      "line": 28,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The path of the scattered seed."
    },
    {
      "line": 29,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The path of mathematical hope."
    },
    {
      "line": 31,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "As the transport pods activated and consciousness-forms dispersed across quantum foam, Zephyr felt the weight of what they had chosen."
    },
    {
      "line": 32,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Not cowardice, as Pazuzu claimed, but perhaps the hardest choice of all—to live with the uncertainty of tomorrow rather than die with the certainty of honor."
    },
    {
      "line": 34,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The calculation matrix exploded in a cascade of light as Anunnaki breach protocols tore through the chamber's defenses."
    },
    {
      "line": 35,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "In the chaos of dimensional displacement, Zephyr caught one final glimpse of Elder Pazuzu and the others, their forms blazing with the fire of final defiance as Anunnaki battle-forms materialized around them."
    },
    {
      "line": 37,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Then he was elsewhere, scattered across the quantum foam with the others who had chosen tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "line": 38,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "In the mathematical space between stars, he felt the echo of their choice rippling forward through time—a choice that would someday birth magic, resistance, and hope on a small blue world circling an unremarkable star."
    },
    {
      "line": 40,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The first act of freedom had begun."
    },
    {
      "line": 42,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "end of chapter 016-the choice third coming"
    }
  ],
